===Prepositional phrase===
{{en-PP}}

# {{lb|en|simile}} [[extremely|Extremely]] [[easy]]; sometimes with a connotation of triumph but at other times with a connotation of being meaningless and unsatisfying.
#: {{syn|en|easy as pie|like taking candy from a baby|Thesaurus:easy}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=April 2 1982|author=w:Associated Press|title=Entrants Gamble For Chance To Stalk Big Game|titleurl=http://news.google.com/newspapers?id=d-YbAAAAIBAJ&sjid=llIEAAAAIBAJ&pg=6967,218982&dq=like-shooting-fish-in-a-barrel&hl=en|journal=The Dispatch|accessdate=18 July 2012|page=20|location=USA
|passage=Opponents contend that the lumbering creatures are so easy to shoot that a moose hunt is a slaughter, not a sport. "It's '''like shooting fish in a barrel'''," they say.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=Oct 24 2003|author=[[w:Ken Johnson (art critic)|Ken Johnson]]|title=Art in Review: Mary Ellen Mark—‘Twins’|titleurl=http://www.nytimes.com/2003/10/24/arts/art-in-review-mary-ellen-mark-twins.html|journal=New York Times|accessdate=18 July 2012
|passage=For a photographer, shooting twins at the annual Twins Days Festival in Twinsburg, Ohio, must be '''like shooting fish in a barrel'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=March 29 2005|author=John S. Doyle|titleurl=http://www.independent.ie/unsorted/features/were-all-sport-crazy-but-for-all-the-wrong-sports-271307.html|title=We're all sport crazy... but for all the wrong sports|journal=Irish Independent|location=Ireland|accessdate=18 July 2012
|passage=Standing on those long straight roads with the speed detection gun was '''like shooting fish in a barrel''', somebody said.}}

